# Licence

Danu is free software under the GNU General Public Licence, version 3 or, at
your option, any later version.

    SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

The full text is in `licences/GPL-3`.

## Why the GPL and not something permissive

Two of Danu's dependencies decide this between them.

`libisofill` is available under either the Artistic Licence 1.0 or the GNU GPL
version 1 or later, because it is a line-for-line derivation of the terrain code
in `ogf-server-scripts`, which is released on the same terms as Perl itself.
Danu exercises the GPL branch of that choice and takes it at version 3. The
Artistic branch is no use here: it does not combine cleanly with the other
dependency.

That other dependency is PySide6, which is LGPL version 3. Combining LGPL-3 with
GPL-3 is explicitly permitted, and GPL-3 is the only version of the GPL it
permits. So GPL-3-or-later is not a preference so much as the one licence that
both dependencies allow at once.

Taking the GPL branch is also what lets Danu carry logic ported from the older
Perl. `danu.checks.zero_line` and the uphill-river check descend from
`OGF::Terrain::RiverProfile` and `OGF::Util::StreamShape`, written by Thilo
Stapff; those terms permit the GPL at any version from 1 onwards, so GPL-3 is
within them and the provenance stays traceable rather than being quietly
laundered.

The rest of the pipeline moved here from `ogf-server-scripts` - the build
scripts, the masks, the water constraints, the checks - is recent work by the
OpenGeofiction administrators and is licensed here by its authors.

